a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Web Frontend may be able to impersonate the context of Customer in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Login / Payment request (spoofing)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>af3385a9-f555-41a1-bd1a-5dfd1d771d92</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T13.1af3385a9-f555-41a1-bd1a-5dfd1d771d929003cae7-f358-45c5-a91f-f347d34dc8c4fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9003cae7-f358-45c5-a91f-f347d34dc8c4</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>4</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>af3385a9-f555-41a1-bd1a-5dfd1d771d92:9003cae7-f358-45c5-a91f-f347d34dc8c4:fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Scripting</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>The web server 'Web Frontend' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not sanitize untrusted input.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Login / Payment request (spoofing)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>af3385a9-f555-41a1-bd1a-5dfd1d771d92</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T13.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S3af3385a9-f555-41a1-bd1a-5dfd1d771d929003cae7-f358-45c5-a91f-f347d34dc8c4fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9003cae7-f358-45c5-a91f-f347d34dc8c4</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>3</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>af3385a9-f555-41a1-bd1a-5dfd1d771d92:9003cae7-f358-45c5-a91f-f347d34dc8c4:fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Customer External Entity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Customer may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Web Frontend. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Login / Payment request (spoofing)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>af3385a9-f555-41a1-bd1a-5dfd1d771d92</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T13.1fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c6ca0821d-50b3-417d-bba6-e0a2b3f549d1222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>6ca0821d-50b3-417d-bba6-e0a2b3f549d1</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>6</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c:6ca0821d-50b3-417d-bba6-e0a2b3f549d1:222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Scripting</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>The web server 'API Backend' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not sanitize untrusted input.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>API request (Tampering)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T13.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5fcf729f1-230a-4f29-81ad-0d6bd5b6d63c6ca0821d-50b3-417d-bba6-e0a2b3f549d1222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>6ca0821d-50b3-417d-bba6-e0a2b3f549d1</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>7</b:Id><b