ing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Admin request (Elevation of Privilege) may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin request (Elevation of Privilege)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R6f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>158</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3:de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Admin Portal</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Portal claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin request (Elevation of Privilege)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T1f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>157</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3:de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Lack of Input Validation for Admin Portal</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Admin request (Elevation of Privilege) may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Admin Portal or an elevation of privilege attack against Admin Portal or an information disclosure by Admin Portal. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin request (Elevation of Privilege)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S2f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>156</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3:de9519a3-ae68-43df-8bd6-952b9b9007c5:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Admin Portal Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Portal may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by Admin. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin request (Elevation of Privilege)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>f3cc7ac5-527a-44f8-8885-7fd45674fbc3</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S1222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>105</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the API Backend Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>API Backend may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to Admin Portal. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S2222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>106</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Admin Portal Process</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Portal may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to information disclosure by API Backend. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the destination process.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S2</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T1222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>107</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Lack of Input Validation for Admin Portal</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Admin response may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to a denial of service attack against Admin Portal or an elevation of privilege attack against Admin Portal or an information disclosure by Admin Portal. Failure to verify that input is as expected is a root cause of a very large number of exploitable issues. Consider all paths and the way they handle data. Verify that all input is verified for correctness using an approved list input validation approach.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R6222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>108</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by Admin Portal</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Portal claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I6222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>109</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Sniffing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Information disclosure happens when the information can be read by an unauthorized party.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Admin response may be sniffed by an attacker. Depending on what type of data an attacker can read, it may be used to attack other parts of the system or simply be a disclosure of information leading to compliance violations. Consider encrypting the data flow.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>I6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D3222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>110</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Process Crash or Stop for Admin Portal</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Portal crashes, halts, stops or runs slowly; in all cases violating an availability metric.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>111</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Flow Admin response Is Potentially Interrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent interrupts data flowing across a trust boundary in either direction.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D4</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E6222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>112</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Admin Portal May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>API Backend may be able to remotely execute code for Admin Portal.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E7222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cbf03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>113</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a:5f9f70b7-1b3e-4cb2-9c73-9b663d4ba7cb:f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in Admin Portal</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into Admin Portal in order to change the flow of program execution within Admin Portal to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Admin response</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>f03d22d4-8155-42ca-9ea2-33ff3bdd1c68</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E5852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c104994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>04994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>167</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1:04994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1:222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Using Impersonation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>API Backend may be able to impersonate the context of Authentication Service  in order to gain additional privilege.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Token issuance</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T13.1852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c104994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>04994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>166</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1:04994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1:222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Cross Site Scripting</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>The web server 'API Backend' could be a subject to a cross-site scripting attack because it does not sanitize untrusted input.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Token issuance</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T13.1</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S3852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c104994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>04994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>165</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1:04994e08-74d6-4369-8c27-259d6f2d20c1:222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing the Authentication Service External Entity</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Authentication Service  may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to unauthorized access to API Backend. Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the external entity.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Token issuance</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>222215b5-d2f8-4616-b88b-07fdb667f53a</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S3</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>T18852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c19314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa86b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa8</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>117</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1:9314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa8:6b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>The User Databse Data Store Could Be Corrupted</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Tampering is the act of altering the bits. Tampering with a process involves changing bits in the running process. Similarly, Tampering with a data flow involves changing bits on the wire or between two running processes.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Data flowing across Credential Lookup (Information Disclosure) may be tampered with by an attacker. This may lead to corruption of User Databse. Ensure the integrity of the data flow to the data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Credential Lookup (Information Disclosure)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>6b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>T18</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R8852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c19314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa86b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa8</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>118</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1:9314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa8:6b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Denies User Databse Potentially Writing Data</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>User Databse claims that it did not write data received from an entity on the other side of the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Credential Lookup (Information Disclosure)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>6b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R8</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D4852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c19314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa86b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>89851dc0-63a9-45b3-90b7-c444e5d4f358</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>9314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa8</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>119</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>852be83c-77e2-4ddb-a694-75f4f74ba2c1:9314f870-c62b-48b1-92ba-6815505c2aa8:6b16e4a0-f88b-46c8-ac5a-2671227f1606</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b: